  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 107 PM CST Sat Nov 21 2026\n\nOne last afternoon of pleasant, record warm weather today, then the \nlate fall cold weather takes over. Some cities will be near or\nwill break the high temperature record this afternoon. Tonight \nthe lows will be dropping only into the upper 40s to low 50s, \nwhich will be warmer than the highs for the new week. A strong \ncold front associated with a low pressure system in Canada is \nexpected to push through starting early tomorrow morning, \nbringing much cooler temperatures and rain. \n\nThe timing for the cold front tomorrow appears to have the rain \nmoving into the western border of the CWA by 12z. Rain will be \nconnected with the front as it moves east across the state, with it \nexiting to the east of IL by 00z Monday. There could be a rumble of \nthunder in some of the heavier showers, but for the most part, \nthunderstorms are not expected. Rainfall amounts won't be drought \nbusting with amounts around 0.25-0.75 inches. \n\nBehind the cold front, much cooler temperatures will be ushered in \nfor the week by the northwesterly winds. Highs in the low to mid 40s \nfor the first half of the week, slightly warming up to mid 40s to \nlow 50s for the end of the week. Lows will be in the 20s each night \nnext week. Take care to have plenty of warm bedding for outdoor\nanimals/livestock and bring in any vulnerable plants if they \nhadn't already been impacted by the last round of freezing \ntemperatures. \n\nThere is still quite a bit of uncertainty with the late week system \nthe differing synoptic models have been depicting the last few days. \nLocation and path of the system shifts with every new run of the \nmodels with differing severity across the various models. The GFS \nhas a much further west reach with the precipitation than the \nEuro does, which brings more snow and rain/snow mix to central \nIL on Wednesday night than the Euro does. We will have to \ncontinue to monitor the trends as we go into the new week. As of\nthis forecast, there is a 10-30% chance of precipitation \nWednesday into Thursday. Stay tuned for the newest information \nwith each forecast run, as this is the busiest travel week of \nthe year.",
